SUMMARY:Moonlit Horseshoe Crab Walk
DESCRIPTION:Grab your flashlights and get ready to behold an annual spring phenomenon: Horseshoe Crab spawning on the Cape May Harbor!  Walk along the shoreline with a Nature Center Naturalist and learn all about Horseshoe Crab ecology and life history. Plus\, help this keystone species by flipping them over while listening to the tale of Red Knots\, an endangered species lovingly nicknamed the “Moon Bird”. \n\n\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION: Children may not participate without an adult. Please bring flashlights (cell phone flashlights work too!). We may walk up to a mile\, over generally level surfaces. Some surfaces may be sandy\, slippery\, or uneven. Please dress for the weather and wear waterproof footwear. \nCOST: $8 children\, $12 adults \n\n\nWHEN: Saturday\, May 23rd\, 8 p.m.-9 p.m. \nWHERE: Nature Center of Cape May (1600 Delaware Avenue\, Cape May NJ 08204) \n\n\nCANCELLATION: NJ Audubon’s CMBO programs are virtually never cancelled. If we cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, all participants will be notified as soon as possible and are eligible for a full refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 48 hours in advance. Sorry\, no refund for cancellations less than 48 hours in advance unless due to health emergencies; however\, registrations can be transferred to another program in the future. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/moonlit-horseshoe-crab-walk/
LOCATION:Nature Center of Cape May\, 1600 Delaware Avenue\, Cape May\, NJ\, 08204\, United States
CATEGORIES:Family Program,Nature Center of Cape May,Nature Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Moonlit-Horseshoe-Crab-Walk.jpg
GEO:38.9452704878;-74.8992712451
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Center of Cape May 1600 Delaware Avenue Cape May NJ 08204 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1600 Delaware Avenue:geo:-74.8992712451,38.9452704878
END:VEVENT
