SUMMARY:Old Mine Rd/Delaware Water Gap
DESCRIPTION:A perennial favorite for many breeding warblers and other songbirds in a beautiful setting during the height of the nesting season. Great roadside birding along the scenic upper Delaware River\, with a wide variety of breeding songbirds\, including Black-billed Cuckoo\, Alder Flycatcher\, Louisiana Waterthrush\, Worm-eating\, Hooded\, & Cerulean Warblers. Led by Scott Barnes and Linda Mack. \nMEETING LOCATION: Meet at the Kittatinny Point Visitor Center. \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/old-mine-rd-delaware-water-gap-9/
LOCATION:Kittatinny Point Visitor Center\, 1 Interstate 80\, Columbia\, NJ\, 07822\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Old-Mine-Rd-Delaware-Water-Gap.jpg
GEO:40.9702057;-75.1282266
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=DESCRIPTION:A perennial favorite for many breeding warblers and other songbirds in a beautiful setting during the height of the nesting season. Great roadside birding along the scenic upper Delaware River with a wide variety of breeding songbirds including Black-billed Cuckoo Alder Flycatcher Louisiana Waterthrush Worm-eating Hooded & Cerulean Warblers. Led by Scott Barnes and Linda Mack. \nMEETING  Meet at the Kittatinny Point Visitor Center. \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1 Interstate 80:geo:-75.1282266,40.9702057
